### Hands-On: Reading Digital Inputs

To read a digital sensor, configure the pin using `pinMode()` and read its state in `loop()`:

```cpp
const int sensorPin = 2;

void setup() {
  pinMode(sensorPin, INPUT_PULLUP); // Activates internal 20kΩ pull-up resistor
  Serial.begin(9600);
}

void loop() {
  int sensorState = digitalRead(sensorPin);
  if (sensorState == LOW) {
    Serial.println("ALERT: Sensor Triggered (Connected to Ground)!");
  }
  delay(100);
}
```

